- ## Decision Criteria
- ### Complexity Scoring
- | Pattern | Score | Example |
- |---------|-------|---------|
- | Architecture design | +10 | "Design a system architecture" |
- | Microservices | +10 | "Build microservices" |
- | Multi-step analysis | +10 | "Comprehensive analysis" |
- | Scalability | +10 | "Make it scalable" |
- | Refactor codebase | +10 | "Refactor entire system" |
- | Methodology comparison | +8 | "Compare approaches" |
- | Performance optimization | +8 | "Optimize performance" |
- | Explain how/why | +5 | "Explain how it works" |
- | Simple syntax query | -5 | "What is the syntax" |
- **Default threshold: 20 points**
- ### Privacy Overrides
- **Always uses primary model (typically local) when sensitive data detected:**
- - API keys (`sk-...`, `api_key`, `API_KEY`)
- - Secrets/Tokens (`secret`, `token`, `bearer`)
- - Credentials (`credential`, `private_key`)
- - Personal data (email, SSN, credit card)
- ## Context Tracking
- Model Router automatically maintains conversation context across model switches. When a conversation transitions from primary to secondary model (or vice versa), the entire conversation history is preserved and passed to the new model.
- ### How It Works
- Message 1 (simple)     → Primary Model  → Response 1
-                                                 ↓
- Message 2 (complex)    → Secondary Model → Response 2
-               ↑                              │
-               ↑                              │
-               │                              └── Context includes
-               │                              └── Context includes
-               │                                  Message 1, Response 1
-           Context Loaded
-           Context Loaded
- Message 3 (simple)     → Primary Model  → Response 3
-               │                                  all previous messages
- ### Starting a Conversation
- # First message - creates a conversation
- # Output: 💡 Continue with: -c abc123...
- ### Continuing with Context
- # Use the conversation ID to maintain context
- python3 skill/scripts/router.py -c abc123... "Now explain while loops"
- # The new model receives the full conversation history
- ### Context Commands
- | Command | Description |
- | Command | Description |
- |---------|-------------|
- |---------|-------------|
- | `-c ID, --conversation ID` | Continue existing conversation |
- | `--show-context -c ID` | Show conversation history |
- | `--list-conversations` | List all conversations |
- | `--no-context` | Disable context tracking |
- ### Example with Context
- # Start conversation
- python3 skill/scripts/router.py "What is Python?"
- # → PRIMARY (ollama:llama3:8b)
- # → PRIMARY (ollama:llama3:8b)
- # → Conversation ID: abc123...
- # Continue with context
- python3 skill/scripts/router.py -c abc123... "Design a system using Python"
- # → SECONDARY (anthropic:claude-opus-4)
- # → Model switch: ollama:llama3:8b → anthropic:claude-opus-4
- # → Context includes previous message
- # Continue again
- python3 skill/scripts/router.py -c abc123... "Simplify the design"
- # → Context includes all previous messages
